{"duration_api_ms":42335,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"98180f02-b761-49e2-8517-bc7372beab81","total_cost_usd":0.3929136,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26823,"cache_read_input_tokens":592408,"output_tokens":2988,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":180},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26823,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":789,"cache_read_input_tokens":58721,"cache_creation_input_tokens":440,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":440},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":2988,"cacheReadInputTokens":592408,"cacheCreationInputTokens":26823,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3929136,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":180,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":26823,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":11,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Both acceptance commands now pass, and PKT-0137 still changes no server code. The finding stands: the server already saves an explicitly closed document without the 5 s wait, but a browser tab close never arrives as an explicit close.\n\n**Both rejections fixed:**\n- **`.theseus/oracle/unit.sh`:** passes (178 passed, 1 skipped). The earlier failure was in the timing-sensitive timeout tests in `tests/unit/request.tests.js`, which this packet doesn't touch.\n- **`bash .theseus/oracle/journeys/save.sh`:** passes. It had failed because `external/sdkjs` was missing from the worktree. I cloned the fork's `theseus` branch from `../.external/https___github_com_BR-Office_br-office-sdkjs.git` into `external/sdkjs`; the Euro-Office mirror only has `main`. Git ignores `external/`, so the clone is not committed. The journey measured 5918 ms p50, of which 5007 ms is the save delay. That is unchanged, as expected with no code change.\n\n**Finding:**\n- **Server side:** when the client sends the `{type:\"close\"}` message, the server already saves immediately (`noDelay = !reason || shutdown`, `DocsCoServer.js` ~2191).\n- **Client side:** the web client sends nothing on unload. Its socket.io library just closes the connection, so a tab close, a reload and a dropped connection all reach the server as `transport close`.\n- **Decision:** treating `transport close` as a final close would break the contract that a user who reconnects within the delay (a reload, for example) still finds the session open. So I made no server change.\n- **Follow-up:** I recorded a request in `.theseus/spawn/` to measure a close driven by the integrator through the API (`asc_coAuthoringDisconnect`). That path should give the expected ~0.85 s save.\n\nThe Executor log and the friction line are updated, `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and `theseus scope-check` is ok. The work is committed in two commits on the packet branch.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- Every browser tab close or reload reaches the server as `transport close` and waits the full save delay. Only the API close skips it.\n- `environment.md` should name the BR-Office mirror that holds the `theseus` branch, or the factory should check out `external/` in every worktree.","ttft_ms":3483,"type":"result","duration_ms":209804,"uuid":"337c5429-991b-4b7f